@592[2]. From proprium, all tend to Hell.

@DP 69. Of himself, man continually tends to the lowest of Hell.

@SE 4652. (Gentiles explored by noticing whether they tend to Heaven or to Hell.)

@AE 238[3]. "They bend their bow." ( = prepared to destroy. @357[21].)

