Striped.; Striatus.
Striation.; Striatura.
Streaks.; Striae.
Stripes, In.; Striatim.

@AC 2492. With such, the callosity appears... striated within. (Compare @HH 466.)

@4156[3]. It is then seen that they are only spotted streaks.

@7747. The influx of the Spirits of Mars was felt as a thin striped rain, which was a sign that they were not in the affection of truth and good; for this is represented by what is striped. See @SE 3885.

@LJCont 77. The Africans appeared in striped garments of linen. They said that such garments correspond to them; and that their women have striped garments of silk. @SE 6095.

@DP 318[7]. They who have confirmed themselves in falsities, are like those who see the striations -striaturas- as on the wall; and in the shade of evening they see that striation -striatim- as a rider, or a man...

@CL 315. The rays twinkled through the clouds in streaks -striatim-.

@SE 1057. Spiritual things are represented by... striated things.

@1058. Under <Spiritual>, see this reference.

@--[end]. Therefore such striated bodies are white; and, if they are striated very thinly, they are transparent.

@1075. The difference of Spirits as to spiritual and celestial things may be inferred from the cortical and striate things of the viscera.

@--. In the vitreous humour there is a cortical, but not a striate substance. In the crystalline lens there are striae, but such as are harder. In other viscera in like manner, Explained.

@1108. In the speech of the celestial... there is nothing harsh or stripy, that is, noisy.

@1109. As soon as there is in it anything stripy, that is, not so flowing... it is not accordant, and a Spirit does not acknowledge it as true; but at once notices discrepancies.

@1797. The Angels of the interior Heaven, when represented to Spirits, appear to them in... a garment with white and black neatly mingled almost in stripes.

@5127[2]. When their interior affections, which are good, fall into this (sensuous state)... their beard appears to them... in little bunches, that is, striped.

@5493[end]. Communication with Heaven seemed to be taken away, which appeared like streaks of light being elevated from him.

@DMin 4708. When this Hell was opened, there appeared a striped snowiness being elevated on high... This striped snowiness was that which exhaled from those pernicious deceits mingled with apparent good.

Strive after.; Affectare.
Affectation.; Affectatio.

@AC 131. The posterity of the Most Ancient Church, which inclined to proprium. @133. @137. @142. @190.

@230. They did not strive after wealth.

@1509. A striving after offices merely to be seen, and to administer the goods of the lord.

@1675[end]. They are not content with their lot, but strive after a vain kind of heavenly joy...

@6924. Affectations of elegance of speech and of learning hide the things themselves.

@DP 117[2]. They... who studiously strive after reputation... for honesty.

@185[end]. They strive after nothing more ardently than to become gods.

@CL 276. Where there is no genuine marriage love it ought to be assumed, so that it may appear as if there were.

Stroke.; Ictus.

