@528. That actual repentance is the Lord... Explained.

@538. That confession ought to be made... and then supplication for aid and power to resist evils. Explained.

@539. Two duties are incumbent on man after self-examination: supplication, and confession. The supplication must be that the Lord will have mercy, that He will give the power to resist the evils of which the man has repented, and will supply the inclination and affection to do good, since man "without Him can do nothing."

@--[2]. Supplication for the remission of sins ought not to be made before the Lord, for the following reasons. Explained.

