@DLove 4. (This) does not transcend my understanding, which is an illustrated rational one.

@DWis 1. 4. It has been granted me to perceive that in the light of the Highest Heaven I was in wisdom; in the light of the Second Heaven, in intelligence; and in the light of the Ultimate Heaven, in knowledge; and when I was solely in natural light I was in ignorance of spiritual things.

@DWis 1. 3. 4. I desire to describe this initial form (of man) as it has been shown to me in the Heavens.

@DWis 1. 7. 1. I have had daily association with Angels and men who had died, from the year 1744 to the present time, a period of nineteen years.

@DWis 1. 3. I was once... brought into the respiration of my spirit, which I then plainly felt to be in accord with that of the Angels of Heaven... On one occasion it was granted the Angels to lead my respiration, and to diminish and successively withdraw the respiration of my body until only the respiration of my spirit remained, which respiration I then perceived by sense. Moreover I have been in the respiration of my spirit whenever I have been in a state like that of Spirits and Angels, and whenever I have been elevated into Heaven; oftentimes I was in the spirit and not in the body; awl at other times in both the spirit and the body. @DLW 391.

@DWis 1. 5. This difference can be known only to one who has been in both worlds... and who can change from the one to the other, so as to be at one time in the one world and at another in the other; and who can by reflection look at one from the other. From this privilege, which has been granted me, I have been instructed in what the natural man is, and what the spiritual man, who is a Spirit.

